    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "FINFORD HOUSE WITH LAKE FRONTAGE TO BUNNAHOW LOUGH\r\n\r\nTHE PROPERTY IS AVAILABLE ON A VARIABLE ACREAGE RANGING FROM APPOXIMATELY 2.42 HECTARES / 6 ACRES TO APPROXIMATELY 6.88 HECTARES / 17 ACRES WITH AN ADDITIONAL C. 1.94 HECTARES / 4.8 ACRES OF LAKE.\r\n\r\nShannon International Airport 40 km, Galway City 55 km, Gort 9 km, Ennis 20 km.\r\n\r\nA charming period house situated in a tranquil setting with frontage and fishing rights to Bunnahow Lough and fantastic views across the surrounding countryside. Conveniently located within easy reach of the M18 motorway to Galway City, Shannon Airport and the M6 in an area of outstanding natural beauty close to The Burren and Wild Atlantic Way where clear water, clean air and green pastureland predominate. \r\nThe property includes approximately 4.8 acres of Bunnahow Lough, well known for its pike and coarse fishing with fishing rights to the entire. There is also a stretch of the Moyree River that borders the property and flows into the lake, both of which are easily accessed by boat from a mooring on the riverbank and a private jetty from the lake shore. Both lake and lands are a haven for wildlife that include many species of birds including swans, duck, woodcock and snipe.\r\nThe house is approached via an impressive avenue through an entrance with stone piers and iron gates that leads to a large gravelled parking area at the rear of the house. Fine mature trees and expansive lawns surround the house providing complete privacy. The house which is full of charm and character has seven bedrooms and five bathrooms, two reception rooms, conservatory, kitchen, utility and cloakroom. The outbuildings include a studio that could be converted into additional accommodation if required (SPP), a boat house, a timber potting shed and garden room.\r\nThe Burren National Park renowned for its rugged limestone landscape, rare wildflowers and unique views is 10 kilometres away and The Wild Atlantic Way with its towering cliffs, vast sandy beaches and some of the finest links golf courses in Europe is 25 km distant. Galway city famous for its hotels, bars, restaurants and racecourse is within an hour’s drive.\r\nThe local town of Gort (9 km distant) has a wide variety of shops, restaurants and bars, a Supervalu, Lidl and Centra, Bank of Ireland, Post Office, primary and secondary schools and sports clubs. Scoil Aine Naofa primary school is 3 km distant.\r\n\r\nOUTBUILDINGS\r\nSTUDIO\r\nStudio Room 7.05m x 4.45m with Mezzanine 7.05m x 1.55m. Ceiling height 4.30m.\r\nSunroom: 4.10m x 2.65m. Double exterior doors. \r\nBOAT SHED: 8.60m x 7.20m.\r\n\r\nTHE LANDS \r\nThe lands which total approximately 17 acres are divided into four paddocks are all in permanent pasture with views and frontage to the lake.\r\nThere are approximately 250 metres of lake frontage and approximately 4.8 acres of the lake is included with the property with fishing rights extending across the entire lake.\r\n\r\nSERVICES \r\nBroadband, well water, broadband, oil fired central heating, sewage treatment plant.\r\n\r\nASKING PRICE\r\nThe House with C. 6 acres & C. 4.8 acres of lake. Asking Price €650,000\r\nThe Entire Property. The House with C. 17 acres & C. 4.8 acres of lake. Asking Price €780,000"
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Accommodation",
        "SortOrder": 1,
        "Content": "ACCOMMODATION C. 255 m² / 2,745 ft² \r\nEntrance Hall: 5.40m x 2.75m. Tiled floor. \r\nSitting / Dining Room: 6.50m x 5.40m. Slate fireplace with cast iron insert and solid fuel stove, timber floor. Double doors leading to conservatory.\r\nConservatory: 5.60m Average x 3.55m. Tiled floor and double doors outside. \r\nKitchen: 6.05m x 3.60m. Fitted cupboards, drawers and work tops with tiled surround and Belfast sink. Rangemaster cooker with oven, grill, gas hob and extractor fan, freezer, fridge and dishwasher.\r\nRear Hallway with rear door: 1.90m x 0.95m. \r\nUtility Room: 3.20m x 1.90m. Fitted cupboards, drawers and work tops, stainless-steel sink, central heating boiler and tiled floor.\r\nCloakroom: 1.90m x 1.65m. Wash had basin, WC and tiled floor. \r\nLiving Room: 3.80m x 3.45m. Fitted shelves and timber floor.\r\nBedroom 1: 3.75m x 3.65m. Built in wardrobe.\r\nEnsuite Bathroom: 2.05m x 1.20m. Shower, WC, wash hand basin, tiled floor and walls.\r\nFirst Floor \r\nLanding: 5.40m x 2.75m.\r\nBedroom 2: 5.15m x 2.65m. \r\nEnsuite Bathroom: 2.65m x 1.05m. Shower, WC, wash hand basin, tiled floor and walls.\r\nBedroom 3: 4.05m x 3.60m. \r\nBedroom 4: 4.00m Average x 3.00m Average. \r\nEnsuite Bathroom: 2.65m x 1.05m. Shower, WC, wash hand basin, tiled floor and walls.\r\nBedroom 5: 5.15m x 2.65m. \r\nEnsuite Bathroom: 2.65m x 1.20m. Shower, WC, wash hand basin, tiled floor and walls.\r\nAiring Cupboard: 1.50m x 1.00m\r\nFitted shelves and hot water immersion.\r\nBedroom 6: 3.50m Average x 2.50m Average. Wash hand basin.\r\nBedroom 7: 3.50m Average x 2.50m Average. Wash hand basin.\r\nBathroom: 3.00m x 2.10m. Bath with shower attachment, WC, wash hand basin, tiled floor and walls."
